# Store every file exactly as it is on disk. No line-ending conversion.
#
# Git on Windows would otherwise check `bin/check.sh` and `bin/run-task.command`
# out with CRLF endings, and a shell script with CRLF fails on macOS and Linux
# with an error that names the wrong thing entirely ("bad interpreter: no such
# file or directory"). This package ships those scripts, so the conversion
# would break the half of the platforms that cannot be tested here.
#
# The Windows launchers (.bat, .vbs) are already CRLF on disk and stay that
# way for the same reason: what is on disk works.
* -text

# Binary, so git never tries to diff or convert them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.onnx binary
